<title>JAPAN: Japan Tobacco shares up on HIV drug move.</title>
<headline>Japan Tobacco shares up on HIV drug move.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan Tobacco Inc shares were up in Friday afternoon trade after news that the company and its U.S. partner will apply for approval in the United States to market a jointly developed drug for treating HIV, the virus that causes AIDS, brokers said.</p>
<p>The shares had added 3,000 yen to reach 803,000 yen by 0349 GMT.  </p>
<p>Japan Tobacco and Agouron Pharmaceuticals Inc which was established in 1984, have been collaborating on the development of the drug, VIRACEPT, since December 1994.</p>
